[01:18:13] [INFO] [step_14_kerr_tep]   Key result:  The Kerr-TEP generalization extends the framework to spinning BHs. Shadow and ISCO deviations are spin-dependent, providing additional discriminating power. The conformal factor cancels in the frame-dragging frequency, but sGB metric corrections modify it at order eta^2. GW150914 ringdown and EHT shadows provide multi-messenger constraints on the coupling.
